properties.statement_tex:
Let $B$ be a ring and let $h,x,y,s\in B$ satisfy
\begin{equation}
  x^2+y^3=hs,\qquad (h,y)=B. \label{eq:base}
\end{equation}
Then the $B$-algebra
\[
  C=B[U,V,W]/\bigl(U^3+hV-x,\,-U^2+hW-y,\,
                     S(h,U,V,W)-s\bigr)
\]
is isomorphic to $B[T]$, where $T$ is an indeterminate.

